-574b-b368-3759760d7d2e" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275219 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(12-7)(-4-(-4))+(7-7)(-6-(-4)) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+(6-7)(-4-(-4))+(3-7)(-2-(-4))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(5)(0)+(0)(-2)+(-1)(0)+(-4)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+0+0-8] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275220 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274876 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275220 1069 "q-149617" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275220 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275220 1071 "Consider the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={6,\\,4,\\,8,\\,6},\\,y={4,\\,7,\\,11,\\,14}\n$$\n\nYou're given that $\\overset{―}{x}=6$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=9.$ Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y).$" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275220 1072 #uuid "f9c47870-1c3c-5cbd-a10d-e30d2edb18f8" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275220 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(6-6)(4-9)+(4-6)(7-9)+(8-6)(11-9)+(6-6)(14-9)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(0)(-5)+(-2)(-2)+(2)(2)+(0)(5)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[0+4+4+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275221 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274648 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275221 1069 "q-149618" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275221 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275221 1071 "Calculate $\\text{Cov}(x,y)$ for the following data sets:\n\n$$\nx={-12,\\,-10,\\,-9,\\,-13},\\,y={-2,\\,0,\\,3,\\,3}\n$$" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275221 1072 #uuid "109d6e14-293a-5a53-8e5d-a21023c4bf8e" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275221 1074 "The (population) covariance of the data sets $x={{x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}}$ and $y={{y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n}}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}$ and $\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}$ are the means of the data sets.\n\nFirst, we need to compute the means:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-12-10-9-13) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-44) \\\\  & =-11 \\\\ \\overset{―}{y} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-2+0+3+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance of our data sets is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-12-(-11))(-2-1)+(-10-(-11))(0-1) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+(-9-(-11))(3-1)+(-13-(-11))(3-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-1)(-3)+(1)(-1)+(2)(2)+(-2)(2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[3-1+4-4] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275222 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274826 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275222 1069 "q-149628" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275222 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275222 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,3]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,8]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275222 1072 #uuid "ba5f3cf2-5db7-5ec1-b7c9-a70950beee5d" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275222 1074 "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}4Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[2,3]$ and $[3,8]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =3-2=1, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =8-3=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n4{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=4\\cdot 1\\cdot 5=20.\n$$" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275223 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274921 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275223 1069 "q-149629" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275223 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275223 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,6]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval $[4,6]$\n\nCalculate  ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275223 1072 #uuid "95f911f2-bf4c-5ce3-aea3-6a41dcf640f1" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275223 1074 "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[4,6].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=6-4=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we can evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=32\\cdot 2=64.\n$$" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275224 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274955 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275224 1069 "q-149631" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275224 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275224 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,5]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ is a partition of the interval 