{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}-3({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275226 1072 #uuid "6ead2a91-4719-5999-bfe0-1edbb8b3c0b2" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275226 1074 "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n-3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[8,9].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=9-8 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})\\,+\\,({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}-(-4)^{2} \\\\  & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n-3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=(-3)\\cdot (-15)\\cdot 1=45.\n$$" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275227 1068 #edb/ref 17592186274882 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275227 1069 "q-149651" 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275227 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533403 17592186045585 true] [17592186275227 1071 "The marginal mass functions of the independent discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are shown below. Given that the corresponding joint probability mass function is $f(x,y),$ fin